##" US public transit from the FTA National Transit Database. Two sources. `transit`: monthly ridership and service for every US agency, 2002 to August 2026 (trips, service hours, recovery since 2019, the Triangle against Sun Belt peers, big vs small agencies). `ondemand_annual`: on-demand service 2022 to 2024 split into ADA paratransit and general-public on-demand (microtransit), with operating spend; use it for any microtransit, paratransit or on-demand vendor question. Playbook views answer buyer questions directly: ondemand_annual -> agencies_scaling_microtransit (who a microtransit company should call first), microtransit_market_size (the money), mostly_paratransit_agencies, paratransit_without_microtransit; transit -> does_restoring_service_bring_riders_back, triangle_vs_peer_metros, nc_agencies_below_2019, goraleigh_138_percent_check. Defaults to North Carolina on dashboards; pick any state. Sources: FTA National Transit Database on data.transportation.gov (8bui-9xvu monthly, ccvf-fykn agencies, wwdp-t4re / ekg5-frzt / uk25-sge7 / i3pw-uwab annual on-demand), public domain, downloaded 2026-10-06; row counts and 2019 / latest-12-month totals match the publisher's API (checked 2026-10-07). Caveat: GoRaleigh's counts change in July 2024 (a counting change, not riders).
## dataset { title="US Transit Ridership (NTD Monthly)" }

import { transit, STATE, AGENCY, MODE_GROUP, SIZE_BAND } from 'transit.malloy'
import { ondemand_annual } from 'ondemand.malloy'

export { transit, ondemand_annual, STATE, AGENCY, MODE_GROUP, SIZE_BAND }
